\title{LaTeX Style Guide}
\author{Ivan Jacob Agaloos Pesigan}
\date{}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

This guide covers \LaTeX{} sources:
\texttt{.Rtex} files and the \texttt{.tex} files they input.
Math is in the math guide; prose voice is in \texttt{.setup/ai/style/manuscript.md}.
Agents follow \texttt{.setup/ai/style/latex.md},
which follows this guide and is changed together with it.

\section{Files}

\begin{itemize}
	\item \texttt{.Rtex} files start with the knitr chunk block (root, knitr, biblatex).
	Chunk options are written \texttt{\% \#| label = "..."}.
	\item Every chunk has a label.
	\item The preamble is in numbered files in \texttt{.setup/latex/preamble},
	linked from rProject.
	\item Manuscripts are \texttt{<project>-manuscript-EDIT-THIS.Rtex}.
\end{itemize}

\section{Line Breaks}

Use semantic line breaks (\url{https://sembr.org}).
Start a new line after every sentence,
and at clause boundaries where it helps:
after a comma, semicolon, or colon;
before a conjunction or a relative clause.
A blank line ends a paragraph.
Prose has no length limit; R chunks keep lines under 80 characters.
The PDF does not change.

Existing manuscripts and talks are reflowed one at a time,
each in a push that changes only line breaks,
at a time the user chooses,
and the text of the PDFs is compared to show that nothing else changed.

\section{Indentation}

One tab inside environments (\texttt{equation}, \texttt{table}, \texttt{itemize}, \ldots).

\section{Citations}

Use \texttt{\textbackslash parencite} and \texttt{\textbackslash textcite} only
(biblatex-apa), with keys from the lib-* libraries.
Do not use \texttt{\textbackslash cite} or natbib.
Talks may also use \texttt{\textbackslash footcite} and \texttt{\textbackslash fullcite}.

\section{Labels}

Labels are \texttt{<type>:<project>-<name>},
with the types \texttt{eq}, \texttt{fig}, \texttt{tab}, \texttt{sec}, and \texttt{app}.

\begin{Verbatim}
\label{eq:manMetaVAR-stage1-dynamics}
\end{Verbatim}

\section{References and Numbers}

\begin{itemize}
	\item Use a non-breaking space before a reference or number:
	\texttt{Equation\textasciitilde\textbackslash ref\{...\}},
	\texttt{Table\textasciitilde\textbackslash ref\{...\}},
	\texttt{Stage\textasciitilde 1}.
	\item Do not type the number of an equation, table, figure, or section;
	use \texttt{\textbackslash ref}.
	\item Do not type a value from R; use \texttt{\textbackslash rinline} or a chunk.
\end{itemize}

\section{Floats}

Figures and tables follow the figures and tables guide.

\section{Tools}

\texttt{make lint} reports (never fails on) citations, labels, non-breaking spaces,
typed numbers, indentation, math, and macros.
It does not check where sentences and clauses break, which would be guesswork.

\nocite{RCoreTeam-2026}

